| `scripts/template_snapshot.py` | The one way a keel doer renders from the checkout as it stands: `snapshot_working_tree` commits the modified and untracked files over a clone in a scratch directory, never touching the checkout's index, and `scratch_env` gives every child a hermetic git config and commit dates pinned to one day, so two snapshots of one tree commit the same sha. Scratch outputs and snapshot destinations are preflighted; escapes raise SnapshotError. | imported by `scripts/canary.py` and `scripts/audit_project.py` | — | Leaves out an untracked symlink, named as not checked, and each path its caller skips; it renders nothing itself. Raises and never ends the process. Not a test helper: `tests/hermetic_git.py` clones the working tree for the suite. | [CONTRIBUTING.md](../../CONTRIBUTING.md) | keel maintainers only |
